course: dictionary
lesson: 5
title: A building with a hard name: abattoir
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An abattoir is a building where animals such as cows, pigs and sheep are killed so their meat can be sold as food. Another word for it is slaughterhouse. You can meet it in news about farming and food.
explain: Context clues help you work out the meaning. «Meat is the muscle of an animal that was killed for food.» The sentence tells you where meat comes from, and the next part explains the place: «in Britain the law says animals at an abattoir must usually be made unconscious first so they do not feel it.» So an abattoir is a place where animals are killed, and the law says they must be cared for properly there.
explain: Abattoir is a noun, so you can have one abattoir or many abattoirs. Some phrases to notice are sent to the abattoir and abattoir worker, which means a person who works in an abattoir.
fact: An abattoir is a noun: one abattoir, two abattoirs.
fact: «Abattoir» and «slaughterhouse» mean the same thing: a building where animals are killed for meat.
fact: In Britain, the law says animals at an abattoir must usually be made unconscious first, so they do not feel pain.
fact: Animal welfare means how well animals are cared for and treated, and it is a big topic in news about farming.
fact: An abattoir worker is a person who works in an abattoir.
exercise: «Meat is the muscle of an animal that was killed for food.» What is an abattoir? | A shop where meat is sold wrapped up | A park where animals can play | *A building where animals are killed for meat | A farm where animals are fed and kept
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the same as abattoir. | warehouse | *slaughterhouse | hothouse | farmhouse
exercise: «In Britain the law says animals at an abattoir must usually be made unconscious first so they do not feel it.» What does this tell you about the law? | Animals must be washed before they are allowed to go outside | Farmers must sell every animal they own | *Animals must usually be made unconscious first so they do not feel it | Animals may go wherever they like inside the building
test: Ruth says, «My dad is an abattoir worker.» What does this mean? | He drives a bus for school children | *He works in a building where animals are killed for meat | He grows vegetables on a farm | He sells ice cream at the seaside
test: Which two words mean the same? | abattoir and butcher's shop | *abattoir and slaughterhouse | abattoir and cattle | abattoir and farmhouse
exam: What is the plural of abattoir? | abattoir's | abattoir-es | abattoires | *abattoirs
